    <statement><p>Given that <m>f(7.2) = -7.7</m> and <m>f(7.4) = -9.8</m>, approximate
<m>f'(7.2)</m>.</p>
<p><m>f'(7.2) \approx</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0001"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-10.5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>For small values of <m>h</m>, 
 <m>f'(c) \approx \frac{f(c+h) - f(c)}{h}</m>.
In this problem, <m>c = 7.2</m>, and <m>h = 7.4 - 7.2 = 0.2</m>.
<m>\displaystyle{  f'(7.2) \approx \frac{f(7.4) - f(7.2)}{0.2}
  = \frac{-9.8  + 7.7}{0.2}
  = -10.5.
}</m></p>
</solution>
  </static>
